We have been informed of the controversy in soc.religion.islam that
involves one of our users, Ahmed Hashem. We have received some e-mail
asking us to take (unspecified) action against our user.

I spoke with Dr. Hashem and he assures me that he is working with the 
moderators mailing list and the news.groups Powers that Be to resolve
this conflict.

We hope this matter can be settled in the appropriate groups by the people 
who are directly involved.

If we had a user who was committing some gross violation of Usenet 
etiquette, (for example mail-bombing, flooding newsgroups, or forging other
users's names) , we would take swift action. However, we do not feel that 
it is our job to intervene in disputes about an individual news group's
management or to pass judgements on whether a moderator is following
proper procedures.

Our user has the right to fight his own battles, as long as our system is
used in a civilized manner. 

