>So then, it is fully permisable to rlogin to another machine that is part
>of CDF?  i.e. Towel, Killozap, Trillian, Jade, etc.  

Yes. 

>And it would also then
>be fully permisable to ftp as well from remote logins?  

If by "ftp from remote logins", you mean the ability to use ftp to reach
CDF from somewhere else (eg. ECF) and transfer files, the answer is yes,
assuming the owner of the CDF account involved is doing the transferring. 
It is not okay to give your password to somebody else so that they can 
access your CDF account. If by "ftp from remote logins", you mean the 
ability to use a CDF account to ftp to other systems and transfer files,
this is also okay as long as you are authorized to access the other system
(eg. anonymous FTP). It wouldn't be okay to try to break into another system
via FTP. 

We don't currently have a rule against using FTP while accessing CDF from a
dialup line. 

>Why aren't users
>able to specify which machine they wish to connect to anymore?

Because we replaced the old terminal server (half.cdf) with a new device
that connects directly to eddie. 

